test diamond Si with one additional electron, symmetry=on

Force/stress accuracy (2026-10-29)
--------------------------------
Use scf_thr=1e-12 and pw_diag_nmax=200 to resolve force and
stress at the existing 1e-4 eV/Angstrom and 1e-3 kbar comparison limits.
The former references shift under tighter CG, Davidson-subspace and PPCG
calculations. The updated scalar reference uses an independent
Davidson-subspace run with scf_thr=1e-14, pw_diag_thr_max=1e-12 and
pw_diag_nmax=200. At these settings, the maximum spread across the
three solvers is 8.53e-14 eV in energy, 0 eV/Angstrom
in the force sum and 9e-06 kbar in the stress sum.
Calibration uses GNU 12.3, OpenMPI 5.0.10, four MPI ranks and one
OpenMP/BLAS thread. Structure, pseudopotential, cutoff, mixing and
acceptance tolerances are unchanged. Timing is not a numerical reference.
